{"name":"Bergamot Orange","hex":"#f59d59","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"bergamot","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A tree of the orange family (Citrus × limon, syn. Citrus bergamia), having a roundish or pear-shaped fruit, from the rind of which an essential oil of delicious odor is extracted, much prized as a perfume.","The fruit from the bergamot tree."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A coarse tapestry, manufactured from flock of cotton or hemp, mixed with ox's or goat's hair."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bergamot"},{"term":"orange","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An evergreen tree of the genus Citrus such as Citrus sinensis which yields oranges (the fruit).","Any round citrus fruit with a yellow-red colour when ripe and a sour-sweet taste; the fruit of the orange tree.\n Specifically, a sweet orange or Citrus sinensis."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having the colour of the fruit of an orange tree; yellowred; reddish-yellow."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/orange"}],"entries":[{"title":"Bergamot orange","blocks":[{"text":"Citrus bergamia, commonly known as the bergamot orange, is a fragrant citrus fruit the size of an orange, with a yellow or green colour similar to a lime, depending on ripeness."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/87/Bergamot_orange_-_whole_and_slice.jpg/330px-Bergamot_orange_-_whole_and_slice.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bergamot_orange","wikidata":"Q109196"},{"title":"Orange (colour)","blocks":[{"text":"Orange is the colour between yellow and red on the spectrum of visible light. The human eyes perceive orange when observing light with a dominant wavelength between roughly 585 and 620 nanometres. In traditional colour theory, it is a secondary colour of pigments, produced by mixing yellow and red. In the RGB colour model, it is a tertiary colour. It is named after the fruit of the same name."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Delicatearch.png/330px-Delicatearch.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Orange_(colour)","wikidata":"Q39338"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/35/Bergamot_orange_-_Cross_section.jpg/500px-Bergamot_orange_-_Cross_section.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/35/Bergamot_orange_-_Cross_section.jpg/1280px-Bergamot_orange_-_Cross_section.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/35/Bergamot_orange_-_Cross_section.jpg/500px-Bergamot_orange_-_Cross_section.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Bergamot orange cross section","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABergamot_orange_-_Cross_section.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/Melito_di_Porto_Salvo_-_Citrus_bergamia.jpg/500px-Melito_di_Porto_Salvo_-_Citrus_bergamia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/Melito_di_Porto_Salvo_-_Citrus_bergamia.jpg/1280px-Melito_di_Porto_Salvo_-_Citrus_bergamia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/Melito_di_Porto_Salvo_-_Citrus_bergamia.jpg/500px-Melito_di_Porto_Salvo_-_Citrus_bergamia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Bergamot tree in Melito di Porto Salvo, Calabria, Italy","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMelito_di_Porto_Salvo_-_Citrus_bergamia.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/e/e3/Be